0.25 w BT/F4 10 Tf0 Tc 0 Tw 316.901 131.75 TD [ (1-)1 (1)] TJ/F7 24 Tf-172.776 491.25 TD (1. Introduction)Tj/F7 14 Tf0 -45.25 TD (1.1. Introduction to Quantity One)Tj/F6 10 Tf18 -21.5 TD (Quantity One)Tj/F6 8 Tf60.654 4 TD (\250)Tj/F6 10 Tf5.977 -4 TD ( is a powerful, \337exible software package for imaging and )Tj-66.631 -12 TD (analyzing 1-D electrophoresis gels, dot blots, slot blots, and colonies.)Tj0 -20 TD -0.015 Tc (The software runs in a Windows or Macintosh environment and has an easy-)Tj0 -12 TD 0 Tc (to-use graphical interface with standard pull-down menus, toolbars, and )TjT* (keyboard commands.)Tj0 -20 TD (Quantity One)Tj/F6 8 Tf60.654 4 TD ( )Tj/F6 10 Tf2 -4 TD (can quantitate and analyze a wide variety of biological data, )Tj-62.654 -12 TD (including radioactive, chemiluminescent, \337uorescent, and color-stained )Tj0 -12 TD (samples acquired from densitometers, phosphor imagers, \337uorescent )TjT* (imagers, and gel documentation systems.)Tj0 -20 TD (An image of a sample is captured using the controls in the imaging device )Tj0 -12 TD (window and displayed on your computer monitor. Image processing and )TjT* (analysis operations are performed using commands from the menus and )TjT* (toolbars.)Tj0 -20 TD (Images can be magni\336ed, annotated, rotated, and resized. They can be )Tj0 -12 TD (printed using standard and video printers.)Tj0 -20 TD (The lane-based functions can be used to calculate molecular weights, )Tj0 -12 TD (isoelectric points, VNTRs, Rf values, and other values. The software can )TjT* (measure total and average quantities, determine relative and actual amounts )TjT* (of protein, and count colonies in a Petri dish.)Tj0 -20 TD -0.288 Tw (The software can cope with distortions in the shape of lanes and bands. Lanes )Tj0 -12 TD 0 Tw (can be adjusted along their lengths to compensate for any curvature or )TjT* (smiling of gels.)Tj0 -20 TD (Irregularly shaped, non-lane-based data can be accurately quantitated using )Tj0 -12 TD -0.066 Tc (the Volume tools.)Tj0 -20 TD 0 Tc (Data captured by the imaging device are stored in a \336le under a user-de\336ned )Tj0 -12 TD (name. Files can be shared among all the Discovery Series\252 software, or )TjETendstreamendobj54 0 obj2250endobj52 0 obj<</Type /Page/Parent 38 0 R/Resources <</Font <</F4 16 0 R /F6 20 0 R /F7 25 0 R >>/ProcSet 2 0 R>>/Contents 53 0 R>>endobj56 0 obj<</Length 57 0 R>>stream
